.NET runtime
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Parts of the .NET runtime's class library, as it is at the v10.0.0 tag, are
ported to .NET Framework 4.8 and compiled into InstallerClean.Core, which every
download carries. They are how a path is read, joined and made full; how a file
or folder is found, read, moved, deleted and listed, and a folder made; how a
search pattern is matched; how a Windows error becomes an exception; how a
registry key is listed; how a command line is quoted for a new process; the
dictionary, sequence, string, stream, ASCII, Math, environment and timing members
.NET Framework 4.8 lacks; and the text of the messages its exceptions carry.

  https://github.com/dotnet/runtime

They are in these files in src/InstallerClean.Core/: Helpers/PathText.cs,
Helpers/FullPaths.cs, Helpers/Win32Marshal.cs, Helpers/RegistryNames.cs,
Helpers/CommandLineArguments.cs, Helpers/Durations.cs, and in Compatibility/,
FrameworkFile.cs, FrameworkFileInfo.cs, FrameworkFileSystem.cs,
FrameworkFileSystemEnumerable.cs, FrameworkFileSystemName.cs,
FrameworkDirectory.cs, FrameworkStreamExtensions.cs,
FrameworkStringExtensions.cs, FrameworkCollectionExtensions.cs,
FrameworkEnumerable.cs, FrameworkEnvironment.cs, FrameworkMath.cs, Ascii.cs,
FrameworkArgumentException.cs, FrameworkArgumentOutOfRangeException.cs,
ConfigureAwaitOptions.cs and TaskCompletionSource.cs.

